      "wages +0.3% m/m for a weak print to stop it Tue Nov 3 US midterm elections Polls: Democrats likely take the House, Senate tighter Historically the market's best stretch of the 4-year cycle starts after the vote; also the date after which US–Iran strikes may resume Mon Nov 2 US ISM Manufacturing PMI (Oct), 10:00 a.m. 54.7 (prev 54.5); prices-paid was 77.9 Prices-paid is the inflation tell Mon Nov 2 + Wed Nov 4 Treasury quarterly refunding Less long-bond issuance, more T-bills expected; chatter about dropping the 20-year Fewer long bonds for sale = support for the 10-year staying under 5% Tue Nov 3 US JOLTS job openings (Sep), 10:00 a.m. 7.1M (prev 7.08M) Demand for workers; a lead on Friday Mon Nov 2, 10:30 p.m. ET Reserve Bank of Australia Hike to 4.85% from 4.60% (88% priced) Global rate cycle still up Wed Nov 4 US ADP private payrolls, 8:15 a.m.; ISM Services PMI, 10:00 a.m. ADP +70K (prev +90K); ISM services 54.7 (prev 54.9) Services is 70%+ of the economy Wed Nov 4 Eurozone flash CPI (Oct) 3.9% y/y (prev 3.8%) Sets up a December ECB hike Thu Nov 5 Bank of England, 7:00 a.m. Hike to 4.00% from 3.75% (98% priced) Pound and gilts (UK government bonds) Thu Nov 5 US jobless claims, 8:30 a.m.; Challenger layoffs Claims about 195K Still very low = labor market tight Fri Nov 6 UMich consumer sentiment (Nov flash), 10:00 a.m. 47.3 (prev 48.0); 1-yr inflation expectations prev 4.7% Sentiment near record lows despite a booming economy All week US–Iran Weekend Qatari- mediated talks; Brent fell under $109 Monday morning Oil above $100 is why the Fed is talking hikes; a deal knocks oil hard, a strike spikes it All week Earnings: Apple, AMD, Palantir, Qualcomm, Arm, Arista (31% of S&P 500 reports); Anthropic October Yardeni's four bars After Alphabet, Amazon, Intel and ServiceNow sold off, the market is punishing anyone who misses",
      "ARR All week Six Fed speakers (Goolsbee Mon; Hammack, Barkin, Logan Thu; Williams, Musalem, Bowman Fri) Any pushback on a December hike December about 80% priced; a dovish surprise moves the 2- year Closing Note: For those of you interested in following the markets, I suggest two websites. ForexFactory.com and tradingview.com. Forex will give you major events on the calendar like Jobs reports, PMI’s, CPI, PCE. Keep up with those and use tradingview to see how those events affect different indexes, the 10yr, oil etc. Information is to the best of my knowledge. Please let me know if you see any errors or if you have any questions This is my first time writing something like this, so I’d appreciate feedback on this and on anything you want to read in the future, for example this is very US centric, if you want to hear about international markets as well, let me know. Again, please reach out with any concerns or questions. Best, Ali Kanji"
