      "The one takeaway: Tech was up 25% by June and is now up 13%. Health care was flat in June and is now up 28%. The two lines crossed for good in mid October, and the last teal drop at the right edge is last week’s Alphabet/Amazon/Intel selloff while health care spiked on Eli Lilly. Something that’s been overlooked has beaten something that’s been in the news everyday over the last six months, and most of the gap opened in the last three weeks.",
